# Compressed circular-unit matrix data for exponent 1831

The proof-package `914 × 914` matrix at `q = 358877` is generated by one
phase function on the cyclic real residue group of order `915`. In cyclic
coordinates its entries are

`M(r,s) = symbolPhase (r+s) - symbolPhase r`.

The 915-value phase and correlation-inverse vectors replace a dense matrix
inverse. The row and column permutations retain the package's original
embedding and circular-unit ordering.

The phase and permutation vectors below were generated from the split-field
root `266093` and checked against every one of the source CSV's `914²`
entries.  The inverse vector was computed in the cyclic Fourier basis and
checked against all 915 correlations.

